6. NICKEL BARRIER PLATING PENALTY (liquid metal requires Ni on Cu; Au must NOT be left on top)
====================================================================================================
plating                                                            3 um           5 um           8 um          12 um    (R'' cm2K/W ; dT at 300 W/cm2)
electroless Ni-P high-P (10-12 % P), k ~ 5 W/mK [LIT]    0.0060 ;  1.8K 0.0100 ;  3.0K 0.0160 ;  4.8K 0.0240 ;  7.2K
electroless Ni-P mid-P (6-9 % P), k ~ 10 W/mK [MEM]      0.0030 ;  0.9K 0.0050 ;  1.5K 0.0080 ;  2.4K 0.0120 ;  3.6K
electroless Ni-P low-P (2-4 % P), k ~ 25 W/mK [MEM]      0.0012 ;  0.4K 0.0020 ;  0.6K 0.0032 ;  1.0K 0.0048 ;  1.4K
electrolytic sulfamate Ni, k ~ 70-90 W/mK [LIT]          0.0004 ;  0.1K 0.0006 ;  0.2K 0.0010 ;  0.3K 0.0015 ;  0.5K
  Rule: a 10 um high-P electroless Ni layer (0.02 cm2K/W) would cost more than the liquid metal itself (0.015).
  Specify electrolytic Ni 3-5 um (or low-P ENi <= 5 um), no Au top coat (Au dissolves into Ga within hours).
  Ga-Ni intermetallic growth is slow below ~100 C; 5 um Ni is the industry floor (PS5 / ASUS ROG practice) [MEM].

====================================================================================================
7. CLAMP FORCE = pressure x contact area   (117 cm2 TTV footprint; 16 cm2 Blackwell-class bare die pair)
====================================================================================================
option           pressure psi          MPa   force on 117 cm2 (N / lbf)    force on 16 cm2 (N / lbf)
grease             15-30      0.10-0.21     1210-  2420 N ( 272- 544 lbf)     165-   331 N (  37-  74 lbf)
pcm                20-40      0.14-0.28     1613-  3227 N ( 363- 725 lbf)     221-   441 N (  50-  99 lbf)
graphite           50-150     0.34-1.03     4034- 12101 N ( 907-2720 lbf)     552-  1655 N ( 124- 372 lbf)
lm                  5-20      0.03-0.14      403-  1613 N (  91- 363 lbf)      55-   221 N (  12-  50 lbf)
in_foil            50-100     0.34-0.69     4034-  8067 N ( 907-1814 lbf)     552-  1103 N ( 124- 248 lbf)
ag_sinter         700-4000    4.83-27.58   56470-322686 N (12696-72546 lbf)    7722- 44128 N (1736-9921 lbf)
d2d_lm              5-15      0.03-0.10      403-  1210 N (  91- 272 lbf)      55-   165 N (  12-  37 lbf)
  retention load   300 N over 117 cm2 =  25.6 kPa =  3.7 psi ; over 50 cm2 =  8.7 psi ; over 16 cm2 =  27.2 psi
  retention load   600 N over 117 cm2 =  51.3 kPa =  7.4 psi ; over 50 cm2 = 17.4 psi ; over 16 cm2 =  54.4 psi
  retention load  1000 N over 117 cm2 =  85.5 kPa = 12.4 psi ; over 50 cm2 = 29.0 psi ; over 16 cm2 =  90.6 psi
  Rule: module retention loads on current GPU/OAM modules are of order 300-1000 N [MEM - verify vs OAM / SXM mech. spec];
  on a 100+ cm2 lid that is only 4-12 psi, below every pad's minimum. Pressure-hungry TIMs (graphite >= 50 psi,
  indium foil) are therefore incompatible with large lids; liquid metal (5-10 psi) and PCM at its low end fit.
  Bare die: limit local pressure to ~0.1-0.3 MPa and avoid edge loading (die-crack) [MEM].

====================================================================================================
8. CTE-DRIVEN SHEAR DISPLACEMENT AT THE DIE EDGE PER CYCLE (free expansion, upper bound)
====================================================================================================
plate material        Blackwell 2-die (~40 mm)      Rubin Ultra 4-die (~60 mm)     15 kW TTV lid-less (108 mm)
Cu              11.5 um (strain  0.5 at 25 um BLT)  17.3 um (strain  0.7 at 25 um BLT)  31.1 um (strain  1.2 at 25 um BLT)
CuW (W85)        3.5 um (strain  0.1 at 25 um BLT)   5.3 um (strain  0.2 at 25 um BLT)   9.5 um (strain  0.4 at 25 um BLT)
CuMo             3.9 um (strain  0.2 at 25 um BLT)   5.9 um (strain  0.2 at 25 um BLT)  10.6 um (strain  0.4 at 25 um BLT)
AlSiC            4.3 um (strain  0.2 at 25 um BLT)   6.5 um (strain  0.3 at 25 um BLT)  11.7 um (strain  0.5 at 25 um BLT)
Si lid           0.0 um (strain  0.0 at 25 um BLT)   0.0 um (strain  0.0 at 25 um BLT)   0.0 um (strain  0.0 at 25 um BLT)
Mo               1.9 um (strain  0.1 at 25 um BLT)   2.9 um (strain  0.1 at 25 um BLT)   5.2 um (strain  0.2 at 25 um BLT)
  Rule: grease at shear strain >= ~0.3-0.5 per cycle pumps out within 10^2-10^3 cycles [LIT];
  solder at strain >> 0.05 fatigues; liquid metal tolerates strain (liquid) but migrates on large bowed areas.
  => Direct-to-die with a copper plate: liquid metal or soft CNT pad only; soldered direct-to-die needs CuW/CuMo/Si lid.

====================================================================================================
9. COST PER PLATE (117 cm2 footprint), order-of-magnitude, material + process adder  [MEM]
====================================================================================================
  liquid metal mass at 25 um over 117 cm2: 1.9 g ; indium solder at 100 um: 8.5 g (In ~US$0.4-0.8/g 2025-26 [MEM])
  grease         US$  2-6               field-reworkable (clean, re-dispense)
  pcm            US$  4-12              field-reworkable (pad is consumable)
  graphite       US$  8-30              reusable, dry, cleanest rework
  lm             US$ 10-30              reworkable by trained tech only; contamination control
  in_foil        US$  8-20              reusable-ish (single compression), dry
  in_solder      US$ 20-45              NOT field-serviceable: plate+package become one FRU
  ag_sinter      US$ 25-60              never reworkable
  d2d_lm         US$ 25-60              reworkable by trained tech; module-level
  microfluidic   n/a (silicon vendor)   not serviceable at interface; fluid connectors at package

